From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:44:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_d2365_charger: Grant 500 mA, not a fixed
 1425 mA

The J172 match data raised the input limit to 0x6c (1425 mA) whenever
the Bellatrix supply reported a source, whatever the source was. A
USB 2.0 port only has to supply 500 mA to a configured device, and a
plain computer port or a bus-powered hub is not obliged to deliver
almost three times that.

On the iPad 6 the limit follows evidence about the source: an
identified charger, USB-C current, BC1.2 or the host's own grant, and
the PMU line withdraws it on unplug within about a millisecond. None of
that exists on the iPad 7 yet. Bellatrix reports presence only, and the
iPad 7 device tree has no PMU event line. Until the source can be
identified and a grant withdrawn on unplug, grant 500 mA, the same
fallback the Tristar charger uses for an unidentified source.

The limit becomes a driver constant instead of board match data: it
follows from USB, not from the board. The guards, readback, attach-
default restore and verified restore are unchanged.

See docs/bring-up/charging/adaptive-charging.md for the reference
design and the steps that lift this limit.

Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_d2365_charger.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_d2365_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_d2365_charger.c
index 63f78303c..8175d4fed 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_d2365_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_d2365_charger.c
@@ -32,6 +32,12 @@
 #define D2365_POLICY_MIN_VOLTAGE_UV	3000000
 #define D2365_POLICY_MAX_VOLTAGE_UV	4350000
 #define D2365_POLICY_INTERVAL_MS	5000
+/*
+ * 500 mA, what USB 2.0 allows a configured device without more evidence.
+ * Nothing on the iPad 7 identifies the source yet or withdraws a grant on
+ * unplug, so a source never gets more than this.
+ */
+#define D2365_FALLBACK_INPUT_LIMIT	0x22
 /* The PMIC applies its attach default shortly after a source attaches. */
 #define D2365_ATTACH_CHECK_MS	100
 #define D2365_ATTACH_WINDOW_MS	15000
@@ -40,13 +46,11 @@
 
 struct apple_d2365_config {
 	u8 handoff_input_limit;
-	u8 charging_input_limit;
 	u8 max_charge;
 };
 
 static const struct apple_d2365_config apple_d2365_j172_config = {
 	.handoff_input_limit = 0x02,
-	.charging_input_limit = 0x6c,
 	.max_charge = 0x34,
 };
 
@@ -373,7 +377,7 @@ static void apple_d2365_charge_policy_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			ret = regmap_write(charger->regmap,
 					   charger->control_base +
 					   D2365_CONTROL_INPUT_LIMIT,
-					   charger->config->charging_input_limit);
+					   D2365_FALLBACK_INPUT_LIMIT);
 			if (!ret)
 				ret = regmap_read(charger->regmap,
 						  charger->control_base +
@@ -386,7 +390,7 @@ static void apple_d2365_charge_policy_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			dev_dbg(charger->dev,
 				"input limit restored after the PMIC attach default\n");
 		}
-		if (input_limit != charger->config->charging_input_limit) {
+		if (input_limit != D2365_FALLBACK_INPUT_LIMIT) {
 			reject_reason = "input-limit integrity";
 			goto out_stop;
 		}
@@ -403,7 +407,7 @@ static void apple_d2365_charge_policy_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	charger->restore_pending = true;
 	ret = regmap_write(charger->regmap,
 			   charger->control_base + D2365_CONTROL_INPUT_LIMIT,
-			   charger->config->charging_input_limit);
+			   D2365_FALLBACK_INPUT_LIMIT);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_write_error;
 
@@ -411,7 +415,7 @@ static void apple_d2365_charge_policy_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			  charger->control_base + D2365_CONTROL_INPUT_LIMIT,
 			  &readback);
 	apple_d2365_cache_input_limit(charger, ret, ret ? 0 : readback);
-	if (ret || readback != charger->config->charging_input_limit) {
+	if (ret || readback != D2365_FALLBACK_INPUT_LIMIT) {
 		if (!ret)
 			ret = -EIO;
 		goto out_write_error;
-- 
